{
  "name": "05-limit-handoff",
  "description": "A run hits a provider limit after one criterion has passed and hands off to the next credential below it, of another provider; that one hits its limit too, so the task is held with credential_limit and waits on the seat's own credential, which resets first; the hold-release timer closes the hold and the run goes back to the seat's own credential; the builder finishes and a reviewer of a third provider passes the task.",
  "covers": [
    "PRD Quality requirements, test 9, and the Handoff milestone: the run continues on another credential with its passed criterion and evidence intact.",
    "PRD Handoff, When a run hits a provider limit: credential.limit_reached, then credential.switched with the app as actor in the same command; credentials above are not tried.",
    "PRD Handoff, When no candidate is available: credential_limit, no Needs you item when a reset time is known, wait_limit names the candidate that resets first (hold.opened carries its credential_id, plan SM-41).",
    "Plan SM-37: the credential_hold_release timer closes the hold at the earliest reset and the task resumes on the seat's own credential with credential.switched.",
    "Plan IF-37 (P-9): the events of a helper report carry the helper's idempotency key as command_id, with the app as actor and the helper as actor_id.",
    "PRD Rules for steps, rule 8 (P-10): a handoff with no hold opens no new step.",
    "PRD Shipped rules: a handoff to another provider adds it to the providers that have built the task, so the reviewer is of a third provider."
  ],
